NOTE: the .hex fixtures below are NOT in this repository. They are a real game's disc
data (Konami) and are not redistributed. Regenerate them from your own dump with:

    scripts/make_adpcm_golden.py "Akumajou Dracula X - Chi no Rondo.chd"

That script holds only the sector NUMBERS, which are metadata, and rebuilds every file
byte-identically (verified against the original capture's MD5s). dma_writes.hex and
nib.hex are pure derivations of sectors.hex and ram.hex respectively, so they need no
separate capture.

Golden ADPCM playback case from beetle-pce-fast, Akumajou Dracula X - Chi no Rondo,
PLAY#8 at emulated frame 25059 (golden/run_adpcm_gold.sh; golden/adpcm_analyze.py).

ram.hex   65536 bytes: ADPCM RAM image when playback started (beetle stores bytes; the FPGA
          stores nibbles, byte k -> nibble 2k high, 2k+1 low)
regs.txt  the game's exact ADPCM register accesses for this play, in order:
          "W reg value" = write $180<reg>, "R reg 00" = read $180<reg>
nib.hex   the 1448 nibbles beetle fed to its OKI decoder, in order
          = 724 bytes from 0x8df8, high nibble first, then auto-stop at the latched length

The R A (dummy read of $180A) while $180D bit 3 is set is load-bearing: cd.vhd only loads its
read address during a pending read. A replay without it starts playback at address 0.
Rondo loads ALL its ADPCM data by DMA from CD ($180B <= 02); none via CPU $180A.
